<title>SINGAPORE: Chemical Industries 1996/97 net falls 9pct.</title>
<headline>Chemical Industries 1996/97 net falls 9pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 7.00  vs   7.71</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)   18.00  vs  19.00</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	10.00  vs  10.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		  32.77  vs  27.26</p>
<p>    Other income	     1.74  vs   1.70</p>
<p>    Interest expense	 4.66  vs   3.06</p>
<p>    Pretax		     7.58  vs   7.36</p>
<p>    Associates		 2.17  vs   2.32</p>
<p>    Tax			  2.45  vs   1.90</p>
<p>    Minorities		(0.30) vs  (0.07)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  0.58  vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - Chemical Industries Far East Ltd said contributions from industrial chemicals is expected to narrow due to competition and the group will continue to look for trading and investment opportunities in the U.K. property market.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
